OOP with C++ – Files and Streams

📚 Unit 4: Files and Streams

This repository contains 16 C++ programs based on File Handling and Streams in Object-Oriented Programming with C++.

The programs cover creating, reading, writing, updating, searching, copying, and managing files using C++.

🎯 Objective

The main objective of this code book is to understand:

- File handling in C++
- Text files
- Binary files
- Input and output streams
- File pointers
- Random access
- File error handling
- Student record management
- Library record management

🛠️ Requirements

- C++ Compiler
- VS Code / Code::Blocks / Dev-C++
- C++17 or later
- Basic knowledge of C++

